```uvl-code
A university course registration system manages student enrollments. All students must register for at least 12 credits. Undergraduate students must select one 100-level Core course, while Graduate students must select a 500-level Seminar. Many courses have prerequisites; for example, 'Advanced AI' requires both 'Intro to AI' and 'Linear Algebra'. Some courses are mutually exclusive, like 'Statistics for Biology' and 'Statistics for Business'. The 'Robotics Lab' course is an optional elective with a hard enrollment cap of 20 students. Finally, the 'Thesis Defense' module is only available to students who have completed 60 credits and passed their 'Dissertation Proposal' review.
```